// EXPECT: [E100]
// EXPECT-TEXT: Error Ln 8, Col 9: a decimal literal has no leading zero: `010` would be octal in C. Write `10`, or `0o10` for octal.
// A decimal literal has no leading zero (Annex A). `010` compiled as 10, where C reads 8, so a
// program ported from C, or a reader who knows C, got another number with nothing said
// (Documentation's grammar audit). Octal is `0o10`.
func main() i32 {
    // a decimal with a leading zero
    x = 010
    return x
}
